      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Softmax Regression, From Scratch\n\nThe classification counterpart of *Linear Regression, From Scratch*: zero-initialised `W` / `b`, a **hand-written softmax cross-entropy** (shift by the row max, exponentiate, normalise, negative-log the true class) and plain full-batch gradient descent. The problem is convex and the recipe is deterministic — the loss curve collapses from `ln(k)` toward zero. Predictions flow into the **Confusion Matrix (Eval)** node, and the rendered matrix below shows exactly which classes get confused. All data is generated in-graph: press **Queue** and watch."
      ]
    },
